cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "done-done: an Agent Skill that forces verification before a coding agent claims done"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Reim-developer"
    website: "https://github.com/Reim-developer"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Reim-developer/done-done"
url: "https://github.com/Reim-developer/done-done"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent-skills
  - coding-agent
  - verification
  - definition-of-done
abstract: >-
  done-done is a prose-only Agent Skill that puts a hard gate between "I wrote
  code" and "I say done." It requires a coding agent to detect the project's
  real verification commands, run them, show the raw output, and either report
  DONE with evidence or an honest BLOCKED report. It ships no runtime code.
